;
; DEED clause profile: (language …) and (identity :thesis …) in
; <repo>_chora.deed, v1.0.0 (DRAFT)
; Prose and rationale: 1-formats/deed/mappings/clade-to-repo-deed.adoc,
; section 3 (the [thesis] and [language] rows), and the owner rulings of
; 2026-11-15 and 2026-11-19 given in the kyX CLADE thread: the chora holds what
; a repo is, what it lives for and what it does in the world (CHORA-SPEC
; 11.1), so a language repo's thesis, paradigm, compile targets and headline
; feature are chora content; the project's design heritage (:inspiration)
; is META.deed's (clauses/meta.abnf), and the repo's internal content
; ordering is CLADE.deed's, once A7 M3 lands.
;
; A CLAUSE PROFILE, not a new grammar. Every rule below is also a `clause`
; or `field` of deed.abnf v2.0.0, so a chora deed carrying them still passes
; deed_lint unchanged. Rules it borrows: string, symbol and token-sep are
; deed.abnf's; symbol-list is common.abnf's. Requires RFC 7405 (%s"..."
; case-sensitive literals).
;
; Where it applies: the top level of a <repo>_chora.deed (head repo-deed and
; that file name), at most once; :thesis inside its (identity …) clause, at
; most once. SEMANTIC (validator-enforced, deed_lint.js --chora-language):
;   * each member at most once; the clause holds at least one;
;   * :paradigm and :compile-targets are non-empty and name each symbol once;
;   * :thesis is a non-empty string;
;   * no other field and no clause inside (language …): a reader that meets
;     an unknown key refuses the clause, never skips it (P-2a).
; The (identity …) clause as a whole has no profile yet (CHORA-SPEC 5.4);
; identity-thesis names only the member this profile adds to it.

language-clause = "(" %s"language" 1*(token-sep language-member) [token-sep] ")"
language-member = ( %s":paradigm"         token-sep symbol-list )
                / ( %s":compile-targets"  token-sep symbol-list )
                / ( %s":headline-feature" token-sep symbol )
                ; :paradigm is the kind of language it is (functional,
                ; affine, typed); :compile-targets what it compiles to;
                ; :headline-feature the one trait it is known for in the
                ; world. All three are symbols, read verbatim from the
                ; source; a source value that is not symbol-legal fails the
                ; translation rather than being respelled.

identity-thesis = %s":thesis" token-sep string
                ; One sentence: what the repo lives for. A member of the
                ; chora's (identity …) clause.
